610
00:30:43,300 --> 00:30:45,969
But if you rescue an American,
it's the law, isn't it?

611
00:30:45,970 --> 00:30:48,388
We aren't here to rescue you.
All right, Paolo?

612
00:30:48,389 --> 00:30:50,890
You're kidding me. You're leaving me here?

613
00:30:50,891 --> 00:30:52,183
<i>Jeokbanhajang!</i>

614
00:30:52,184 --> 00:30:53,351
{\an8}[Jeokbanhajang] The person at fault blames
or scolds someone who has done no wrong.

615
00:30:53,352 --> 00:30:56,354
{\an8}- You want us to take you? Are you crazy?
- He didn't mean it.

616
00:30:56,355 --> 00:30:58,022
You know what's going on out there?

617
00:30:58,023 --> 00:30:59,524
No, no! Stop, stop, stop, stop.

618
00:30:59,525 --> 00:31:00,775
Stop, stay there.

619
00:31:00,776 --> 00:31:04,112
- I think the pills knocked him out.
- I think he really was asleep.

620
00:31:04,113 --> 00:31:05,322
Paolo had no idea.

621
00:31:05,864 --> 00:31:08,158
Paolo. Why, why, why, why?

622
00:31:08,617 --> 00:31:11,328
Just answer the phone.
I need to get out.

623
00:31:12,246 --> 00:31:14,039
[whimpers] Help me.

624
00:31:17,960 --> 00:31:19,253
[zombie snarls]

625
00:31:19,878 --> 00:31:22,089
[whimpers] Shit, shit, shit, shit.

626
00:31:27,344 --> 00:31:29,470
- [grunts]
- [engine revving]

627
00:31:29,471 --> 00:31:30,639
[grunting]

628
00:31:32,349 --> 00:31:34,351
[whimsical music playing]

629
